HDM - Role-based DM powers

Assigned builders:
  hdm goto <room>                      Enter an existing assigned room.
Admin and owner:
  hdm goto <room>                      Teleport yourself (room 1-8999).
  hdm restore                          Restore your own current HP and mana.
Owner only:
  hdm bring <character>                Summon an online lower-role character.
  hdm restore <character>              Restore an online lower-role character.

The founder and other owners cannot be targeted by another owner. Explicitly
naming yourself is allowed for an owner. Teleporting a character in combat
or possessing a monster is refused. Maximum HP/mana, class, level, spells,
gold and XP do not change. Restored characters should save afterward.

Roles and ranges are checked for every action. Use hbuild unassign to remove
range access and hstaff revoke to remove role powers; neither changes class.
Authorized attempts are recorded as powertry in hstaff audit before effects.
These tools provide the listed powers, not blanket access to legacy * DM
commands, account deletion, forced commands or Linux/server controls.
